Verify emails in real-time with Emailable.

== Description ==

Verify emails in real-time with Emailable.

Integrate with Emailable's email verification API through this official plugin. Reduce spam and increase the quality of your signups by verifying emails directly from any form.

This is compatible with all major WordPress Forms and plugins that use the is\_email function to validate email addresses. 

This includes, but is not limited to:

- WordPress's default registration and comment forms
- WooCommerce's registration and checkout form
- Gravity Forms
- Contact Form 7
- Ninja Forms
- Jetpack Forms

Emailable's verification includes:

- Disposable Email Detection
- Accept-All Email Detection
- MX Record Detection
- SMTP Provider Details
- Misspelled Domain Detection
- Syntax Validation
- Domain Validation
- SMTP Verification
- Email Deduplication
- Role Email Detection
- Free Email Detection
- Email Quality Score
- Anti-Greylisting Technology

To use this plugin, [sign up for a free Emailable account](https://app.emailable.com/signup/), create an API key. All new signups will receive 250 free credits. 

What makes Emailable special?

- Best in class performance: 30k emails verified per minute
- Most Advanced Email Detection: Free, No Reply, Role, Accept-All, Disposable, and Mailbox Full
- [99%+ Deliverability Guarantee](https://emailable.com/guarantee/)
- 99.99% Uptime
- 24/7 Support
- SOC 2 Type II certified
- GDPR, Privacy Shield, CCPA, and LGPD compliant

See more information about data privacy in the links below:

- [Emailable's Terms of Service](https://emailable.com/terms-of-service/)
- [Emailable's Privacy Policy](https://emailable.com/privacy-policy/)
- [Emailable's Data Protection Agreement](https://emailable.com/data-processing-agreement/)
- [Emailable's Anti-Spam Policy](https://emailable.com/anti-spam-policy/)

== Installation ==

1. Unzip the downloaded .zip file.
2. Upload the Emailable plugin folder into the `wp-content/plugins/` directory of your WordPress site.
3. Activate `Emailable` from Plugins menu

= Configuration =
Emailable will add a new setting menu page with setting name "Emailable". There you will be able to set the API Key, Allowed States, Allowed Filters and Custom Alert Messages.

